The rewrite keeps the same logic in a more compact form. It merges the two early-return checks into one condition: if `subFieldIndex` is `0xFFFF`, the `||` short-circuits, so `GetNumSubFields()` is still skipped, as before. It also hints that the subfield pointer is usually non-null. Any speedup is likely to be small.

```cpp
FIT_FLOAT64 FieldBase::GetOffset(const FIT_UINT16 subFieldIndex) const
{
    if ((subFieldIndex == 0xFFFF) || (subFieldIndex >= GetNumSubFields()))
        return GetOffset();

    const auto subfield = GetSubField(subFieldIndex);
    if (__builtin_expect(subfield != NULL, 1))
        return subfield->offset;
    return 0.0;
}
```